<title>FINLAND: Kesko extends losses, hits five-month low.</title>
<headline>Kesko extends losses, hits five-month low.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish wholesaler and retailer Kesko Oy extended losses in moderately active trade on Tuesday on reports that the European Commission was expected to reject its acquisition of Tuko, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1200/1000 GMT, Kesko traded at 62.00 markka -- its lowest since June 14 -- down 3.00 markka or more than four percent. Trade was 8.7 million markka, which is quite active for Kesko.</p>
<p>Brokers saw scope for more losses in Kesko until there is a clear decision from the EU about Kesko's Tuko acquisition.</p>
<p>The Commission has expressed fears the deal would give Kesko a dominant market position. --Helsinki +358-9-680 50 248</p>
